      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "The closest structural analogue, CC-292, is an acrylamide-containing 2-aminopyrimidine kinase inhibitor and demonstrated excellent oral bioavailability in a human Phase IA study, directly supporting high F for the query's similar covalent inhibitor scaffold.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C01"],
      "claim": "Deucravacitinib, a small-molecule kinase inhibitor with an aminopyrimidine-related core, showed 99% absolute oral bioavailability in healthy subjects, supporting high oral absorption for this chemical class.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "Brepocitinib, another kinase inhibitor, had approximately 75% absolute oral bioavailability in humans, consistent with high F for the query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C02"],
      "claim": "Golidocitinib showed >80% oral bioavailability in healthy participants based on a radiolabeled mass balance study, reinforcing high F among related kinase inhibitor scaffolds.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is an acrylamide-containing 2-aminopyrimidine kinase inhibitor with features consistent with good permeability and oral absorption. All relevant experimental analogues, including the closest CC-292 scaffold and other kinase inhibitors, show human oral bioavailability well above the 20% threshold (41–99%). Therefore, high bioavailability is strongly supported.",
